# Deploy after each request

When you finish substantive work in this repo (code fixes, features, CSS, or anything that affects the live site), **deploy to production right away** in the same turn. Do not wait for a separate "deploy" message.

## Steps (safe — no wipe before upload)

1. `npm run build` in the project root.
2. `npm run deploy:vps` (or `node scripts/deploy-vps.mjs` after build).
   - Requires SSH key (Mac: `~/.ssh/bb_deploy_key`, Windows: `C:\Users\miche\OneDrive\Documents\Oracle Keys\ssh-key-2026-03-25.key` via `BB_DEPLOY_KEY`).
   - Host: `ubuntu@129.151.144.92`, remote dir: `/home/ubuntu/bytebuddies`.
3. Script verifies `dist/index.html`, runs `verify-dist-index` + `write-bb-entry`, **rsync --delete** (no `rm -rf` on the server), then checks origin serves `/`.

**Do not** run `rm -rf /home/ubuntu/bytebuddies/*` before rsync — a partial upload leaves the site 404 until a full sync completes.

## Exceptions

- Skip deploy if the user explicitly says not to deploy, or the change is docs-only and they asked not to.
- If SSH/SCP fails (key missing, network), report the error and what succeeded (e.g. build OK).

Live site: https://bytebuddies.technology/
